# 2026-04-19 15:12:19.524610
+Implement the endpoint:
+
+GET /<db>/api/companies/<ticker>/records/monthly
+
+Requirements:
+- Check if the company exists in {db}.companies.
+  - If not found → return 404.
+- Query ALL stock records for the given ticker from {db}.stocks.
+- Cassandra does NOT support GROUP BY on clustering columns, so:
+  - You MUST compute monthly averages in Python.
+- For each record:
+  - Extract month in format "YYYY-MM"
+  - Group by month
+  - Compute average of "high" values per month
+
+Edge cases:
+- If Cassandra returns an empty partition row (NULL fields), ignore it.
+- If no valid records exist → return []
+
+Response format MUST match MySQL version exactly:
+[
+  {"month": "YYYY-MM", "avg_high": ...},
+  ...
+]
+
+After implementing:
+- Rebuild and restart the service if needed.
+- Run pytest.
+- Fix any mismatches in formatting, ordering, or float precision if tests fail.

